---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import SectionIntro from '../components/SectionIntro.astro';
import MovementSection from '../components/MovementSection.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
import SiteCta from '../components/SiteCta.astro';
import EditorialPhoto from '../components/EditorialPhoto.astro';
import { withBase } from '../data/site';
import walkingThreshold from '../assets/images/editorial/editorial-walking-threshold.png';
import candlePlaster from '../assets/images/editorial/editorial-candle-plaster.png';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The She Who Remembers Path | She Who Remembers"
  description="The philosophy behind the work: sovereignty, shadow, embodiment, living expression, and legacy. A path for women returning to self-trust."
>
  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="The She Who Remembers path" headingLevel="h1">
        <p>
          This is not a curriculum to complete. It is a sequence of inner movements many women
          recognize once they have language for them. You may enter at any point. The path is
          described here so the work has a spine, not so your life has to match a syllabus.
        </p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="photo-breath">
        <EditorialPhoto
          src={walkingThreshold}
          variant="walking"
          alt="A woman seen from behind walks through an open doorway into warm daylight."
        />
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <MovementSection
        roman="I"
        title="The Awakening"
        subtitle="Reclaiming Sovereignty"
        question="Where have I stopped consulting myself?"
      >
        <p>
          Awakening, here, is rarely cinematic. It looks like catching yourself mid-sentence and
          noticing that the yes you just offered did not come from you. It looks like identity
          that has been organized around usefulness, around being the one who can, around a
          version of power that never required your inner vote.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sovereignty is not isolation. It is the return of authorship: in how you use intuition,
          how you stand in sisterhood without disappearing, how creativity and resilience stop
          being performances and become sources. In real life this can be as ordinary as pausing
          before you agree, or as large as realizing the story you have been living was written
          in someone else's hand.
        </p>
      </MovementSection>

      <Divider />

      <MovementSection
        roman="II"
        title="The Descent"
        subtitle="Meeting What You Were Told to Hide"
        question="What have I exiled in order to remain acceptable?"
      >
        <p>
          What gets sent underground does not vanish. Jealousy, anger, desire, shame, the body's
          unread signals, the boundary you swallowed: they wait. They run the schedule from
          beneath the floorboards: sudden heat, sudden collapse, a no that arrives too late and
          too sharp.
        </p>
        <p>
          These experiences are not explored so they can control your life. They are explored so
          they no longer have to control it from underground. The descent is not an invitation to
          live inside the wound. It is a refusal to pretend the exiled parts are gone.
        </p>
      </MovementSection>

      <div class="photo-breath photo-breath--candle">
        <EditorialPhoto
          src={candlePlaster}
          variant="candle"
          alt="A single candle burns on a plaster ledge in a dark room."
        />
      </div>

      <Divider />

      <MovementSection
        roman="III"
        title="The Embodiment"
        subtitle="Becoming Legible to Yourself"
      >
        <p>
          Insight is not embodiment. A person can intellectually understand every pattern and
          still repeat it Tuesday afternoon. It shows up in the tone of a reply, in the way the
          shoulders lift before a hard conversation, in the yes that leaks out before the body
          has been asked.
        </p>
        <p>
          Embodiment is slower and more specific: breath that is allowed to finish, voice that
          does not rush to make itself palatable, presence that can stay when it would be easier
          to manage the room. It shows up in choices and in relational behavior, not in a
          vocabulary of awakening. You become legible to yourself when the inner signal and the
          outer life stop arguing.
        </p>
      </MovementSection>

      <Divider />

      <MovementSection
        roman="IV"
        title="The Ascent"
        subtitle="From Personal Work to Living Expression"
      >
        <p>
          Eventually healing stops being the center of identity. Life returns. Not because the
          work was a phase you outgrew, but because the work did its job: it made more of you
          available for living.
        </p>
        <p>
          Ascent looks like creating again. Leading without abandoning your own nervous system.
          Relationships that can bear honesty. Contribution that is not a rescue mission.
          Self-correction without self-contempt. Community that does not require you to stay
          small. Inherited patterns noticed in time to choose differently: not perfectly,
          differently.
        </p>
      </MovementSection>

      <Divider />

      <MovementSection
        roman="V"
        title="The Legacy"
        subtitle="What Will Live Because You Lived?"
      >
        <p>
          Legacy does not necessarily mean fame, followers, motherhood, or public visibility. It
          can be quieter than that and still be exact: lived wisdom handed to one person who
          needed it, a family pattern interrupted, a body of work made, a way of being in a room
          that gives other people permission to tell the truth.
        </p>
        <p>
          Mentorship, creation, contribution, ordinary influence: these are forms of
          continuation. The question is not how large the life looks from a distance. The
          question is what continues because someone became conscious.
        </p>
      </MovementSection>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <SiteCta
    heading="If the path is the map, the courses are doors."
    primary={{ label: 'Explore Courses & Experiences', href: withBase('/courses') }}
    secondary={{ label: 'Begin Here', href: withBase('/begin-here') }}
  >
    <p>
      You do not have to walk every movement in order. If you already know the threshold you are
      standing on, start there.
    </p>
  </SiteCta>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .photo-breath {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .photo-breath--candle {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>
